<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karlovac</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karlovac is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, at the meeting of the Kupa, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korana">Korana</a>, Mrežnica and Dobra rivers. It was founded in 1579 by Archduke Charles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> as a star-shaped fortress of the Military Frontier against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and named after him. It later grew into a trading town on the routes from the Pannonian plain to the Adriatic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karlovac.jpg" alt="Karlovac" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bukovacka · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karlova%C4%8Dka_zvijezda-_Izvor-_Digitalni_Tisak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
